<script>
import askReportSource from 'crm/src/ops/askReport.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import draftReportSource from 'crm/src/ops/draftReport.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import AssistedReport from 'crm/src/ops/lib/AssistedReport.abide'
import assistedReportSource from 'crm/src/ops/lib/AssistedReport.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import assistedReportTestSource from 'crm/src/ops/lib/AssistedReport.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import ReportProblem from 'crm/src/ops/lib/ReportProblem.abide'
import reportProblemSource from 'crm/src/ops/lib/ReportProblem.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import reportProblemTestSource from 'crm/src/ops/lib/ReportProblem.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import listReportsSource from 'crm/src/ops/listReports.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import sendStatementSource from 'crm/src/ops/sendStatement.handler.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
import Snippet from '#src/lib/Snippet.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="A failed call is reported from its trace, in words the person reads first">
        <Example
            id="report"
            title="`report` — a draft of what failed, sent to `onReport`"
            summary="Emailing a statement fails, and the page keeps the failed call's trace. Report this opens the draft on it: write what went wrong, read everything that will be sent, and send it."
            files={{
                'src/ops/lib/ReportProblem.abide': reportProblemSource,
                'src/ops/sendStatement.handler.ts': sendStatementSource,
                'src/ops/listReports.handler.ts': listReportsSource,
                'src/ops/lib/ReportProblem.test.ts': reportProblemTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <ReportProblem />
        </Example>

        <p><code>onRefusal</code> hands the page the trace of every call that failed, and
            <code>report</code> starts a draft from it. <code>open()</code> shows it in abide's own
            dialog, with every word that will be sent above the Send button, and settles
            <code>true</code> once it is sent. A page that draws its own binds
            <code>summary</code> and <code>description</code>, shows <code>markdown</code>, and
            calls <code>send()</code>.</p>

        <p>Where a report goes is the server's to say, in <code>onReport</code>. The CRM keeps
            each one for the browser that sent it; an app posts it to its tracker, its inbox or its
            support desk:</p>

        <Snippet source={listReportsSource} path="src/ops/listReports.handler.ts" from={['onReport(']} />

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>What a draft holds</th><th>Where</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td>the page's newest log lines</td><td>in every browser</td></tr>
                <tr><td>the server's lines for its trace</td><td>in the native app's window, and on a server</td></tr>
                <tr><td>the app's version, the user agent and the route</td><td>everywhere</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p>Anywhere else the trace is enough: the server's lines are already the app's, in its
            logs or its tracing, under the same id. The principal secret and every
            <code>password</code> field of the config are taken out of every line before it leaves
            the server, and out of every report before <code>onReport</code> sees it. With no
            <code>onReport</code> filed, a send is refused.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="An assistant fills in a draft that only the person sends">
        <Example
            id="report-assistant"
            title="`resultsOf` — what the assistant wrote, put in the draft"
            summary="Emailing a statement fails, and the page drafts a report on it. Ask the assistant: it reads the draft and fills in the summary and description. Review and send opens it, written, with nothing sent yet."
            files={{
                'src/ops/lib/AssistedReport.abide': assistedReportSource,
                'src/ops/draftReport.handler.ts': draftReportSource,
                'src/ops/askReport.handler.ts': askReportSource,
                'src/ops/lib/AssistedReport.test.ts': assistedReportTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <AssistedReport />
        </Example>

        <p>The assistant is handed the draft's <code>markdown</code>: what the person will read
            before sending, secrets already taken out, and nothing more. In the native app's window
            that holds the server's lines for the trace too, which is what it reads to say what went
            wrong. Its one tool is <code>draftReport</code>, a handler that hands back what it was
            given, and the page puts each answer in the draft:</p>

        <Snippet source={assistedReportSource} path="src/ops/lib/AssistedReport.abide" from={['async function ask(']} />

        <p>No tool sends a report, so the person always does. The CRM's model is recorded, so the
            card answers the same way every time; <code>provider.claudeCode()</code> in its place is
            the visitor's own Claude Code.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
